*EXP: 6*

Experiment 6 : Dynamic Memory Allocation and Memory Usage

Theory:
- stdlib.h: Header file providing functions for memory allocation and program termination.
- unistd.h: Header file providing access to operating system functions.
- argc: Represents the number of command-line arguments.
- atoi(): Converts a string into an integer.
- malloc(): Dynamically allocates memory during program execution.
- free(): Releases dynamically allocated memory.
- free -h: Displays system memory usage in human-readable format.
- watch -n 1 free -h: Displays updated memory usage every second.

commands
nano exp6.c
gcc exp6.c -o exp6
./exp6 100
free -h
watch -n 1 free -h
